Support for the PowerPC guest (B32_PPC). Four things Bridge32 needs from the
ppc target that Unicorn 2.1.4 lacks:

- tb_page_has_code (unicorn-fast-writes.patch) gets a per-target name, since
  a ppc build links the ppc and ppc64 targets into one archive.
- mftb and mfspr 268/269 read the host's monotonic clock at 25 MHz. Unicorn
  compiles them as plain SPR reads that stay 0, because it has no virtual
  clock and never sets up the time base.
- The AltiVec registers VR0-VR31, VSCR and VRSAVE are readable and writable
  (VRn as 16 bytes, most significant first, as stvx stores them).
- XER reads and writes include SO, OV and CA, which QEMU keeps in fields of
  their own, so a saved and restored context keeps its carry.

Applied by CMakeLists.txt at configure time.
